#: 562cf791c513452499d18a61164a9118
msgid "sys-gui-gpu"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:66
#: c43e27cefd8341feb3c8de44d7e12100
msgid "In ``dom0``, enable the formula for ``sys-gui-gpu`` with pillar data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:81
#: a8af2bc8f6fa4085aca5843dbea66363
msgid "You can now disable the ``sys-gui-gpu`` formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:88
#: 24c8abe0a6524a849089c6350c75df81
msgid ""
"One more step is needed: attaching the actual GPU to ``sys-gui-gpu``. This "
"can be done either manually via ``qvm-pci`` (remember to enable permissive "
"option), or via:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:95
#: 6679eb7d048d4f32bf4f429a0f9a23f2
msgid ""
"The latter option assumes Intel graphics card (it has hardcoded PCI "
"address). If you don’t have Intel graphics card, please use the former "
"method with ``qvm-pci`` (see :doc:`How to use PCI devices </user/how-to-"
"guides/how-to-use-pci-devices>`)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:97
#: 65d9d681c32e47d196cc074f29ec4d29
msgid ""
"**Note:** Some platforms can have multiple GPU. For example on laptops, it "
"is usual to have HDMI or DISPLAY port linked to the secondary GPU (generally "
"called *discrete GPU*). In such case, you have to also attach the secondary "
"GPU to ``sys-gui-gpu`` with permissive option."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:99
#: 920798adaa3d450c9f3c3d67ec5b5a14
msgid ""
"At this point, you need to reboot your Qubes OS machine in order to boot "
"into ``sys-gui-gpu``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:101
#: 0fd557d4fc064ad5b2d01a4134bf472e
msgid ""
"**Note:** For some platforms, it can be sufficient to shutdown all the "
"running qubes and starting ``sys-gui-gpu``. Unfortunately, it has been "
"observed that detaching and attaching some GPU cards from ``dom0`` to ``sys-"
"gui-gpu`` can freeze computer. We encourage reboot to prevent any data loss."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:103
#: ec961175f1df4e0298f27c37b844f681
msgid ""
"Once, ``lightdm`` is started, you can log as ``user`` where ``user`` refers "
"to the first ``dom0`` user in ``qubes`` group and with corresponding "
"``dom0`` password. A better approach for handling password is currently "
"discussed in `QubesOS/qubes-issues#6740 <https://github.com/QubesOS/qubes-"
"issues/issues/6740>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:106
#: 23709556eeeb49a8b4522d46042470d6
msgid "VNC GUI domain (``sys-gui-vnc``)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:109
#: aeb836c479b746eab09d41710a5f9bd6
msgid ""
"Here, we describe how to setup ``sys-gui-vnc`` that we call a *remote* GUI "
"domain or referenced as *with a virtual server* in `GUI domain <https://www."
"qubes-os.org/news/2020/03/18/gui-domain/>`__."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:111
#: b4bcdd1a5a72456daf563ecf5ad3d63e
msgid "|sys-gui-vnc|"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:213
#: 09b6a5373f8e4403baee9d274c003bed
msgid "sys-gui-vnc"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:113
#: 56c2ac304a8a4d759eac2beef8427fa8
msgid "In ``dom0``, enable the formula for ``sys-gui-vnc`` with pillar data:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:128
#: a54bd8a7d37f4e9180bdb5bfc9d6aa63
msgid "You can now disable the ``sys-gui-vnc`` formula:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:135
#: b63c6a2370ee4ab5aec78877f9d9653e
msgid ""
"At this point, you need to shutdown all your running qubes as the "
"``default_guivm`` qubes global property has been set to ``sys-gui-vnc``. "
"Then, you can start ``sys-gui-vnc``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:142
#: 2694eac0bf634bf685c33ff57699f27c
msgid ""
"A VNC server session is running on ``localhost:5900`` in ``sys-gui-vnc``. In "
"order to reach the ``VNC`` server, we encourage to not connect ``sys-gui-"
"vnc`` to a ``NetVM`` but rather to use another qube for remote access, say "
"``sys-remote``. First, you need to bind port 5900 of ``sys-gui-vnc`` into a "
"``sys-remote`` local port (you may want to use another port than 5900 to "
"reach ``sys-remote`` from the outside). For that, use ``qubes.ConnectTCP`` "
"RPC service (see :doc:`Firewall </user/security-in-qubes/firewall>`. Then, "
"you can use any ``VNC`` client to connect to you ``sys-remote`` on the "
"chosen local port (5900 if you kept the default one). For the first "
"connection, you will reach ``lightdm`` for which you can log as ``user`` "
"where ``user`` refers to the first ``dom0`` user in ``qubes`` group and with "
"corresponding ``dom0`` password."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:144
#: f324570994ea49adaae22847532b48d1
msgid ""
"**Note:** ``lightdm`` session remains logged even if you disconnect your "
"``VNC`` client. Ensure to lock or log out before disconnecting your ``VNC`` "
"client session."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../user/advanced-topics/gui-domain.rst:146
#: c6a37b073fc449cea1b7032d3db5fd0e
msgid ""
"**WARNING**: This setup raises multiple security issues: 1) Anyone who can "
"reach the ``VNC`` server, can take over the control of the Qubes OS machine, "
"2) A second client can connect even if a connection is already active and "
"potentially get disconnected, 3) You can get disconnected by some unrelated "
"network issues. Generally, if this ``VNC`` server is exposed to open "
"network, it must be protected with some other (cryptographic) layer like "
"``VPN``. The setup as is, is useful only for purely testing machine."
msgstr ""

